  "opportunity_id": "proc_80d81094a2",
  "source": "content_cluster",
  "title": "Monthly gas nominations emailed in free text for Morgan's Point and Josey Ranch",
  "task_class": "gas_nomination",
  "label_mechanical": "Gas nomination and scheduling: submit monthly / nomination / gas",
  "narrative": {
    "what_happens": "Ahead of each new gas month, a counterparty contact emails the logistics desk the plant's nomination volumes for the coming month. Two recurring streams are visible: EGPFC nominating natural gas requirements for the MTBE Plant at Morgan's Point, and an estimated Josey Ranch nomination stating the HPL volume to be effective on the first of the month. The volumes arrive as prose and a short table in the body of an ordinary email rather than through a system, and the desk is expected to take them from the message and act on them. Occasionally a follow-up email revises the figures, citing verbal authority from a named person. The exemplars do not show what the desk does downstream, so where the numbers are keyed is not visible in this evidence.",
    "where_it_stalls": "The nomination is not self-contained: one sender is still chasing a missing transport number from a named person on the recipient's side before the nomination can be complete, and a later message restates volumes as a revision authorised verbally by an individual on a specific morning. So a submission can sit incomplete pending a detail held by someone else, and an already-submitted month can be re-cut and re-sent by hand, with the audit trail living only in the email body. With email carrying nearly all of these messages and no shared form, there is nothing that validates the figures at the point of sending.",
    "why_it_recurs": "Nominations are set per gas month with an effective date on the first, so the same submission is composed again for every month across the period observed.",
    "automation_opportunity": "A fixed submission form or structured template per plant that captures volume, effective date, meter and transport number, rejects submission until required fields are present, and posts the values straight to the scheduling record \u2014 with revisions entered as a new dated version against the original rather than as a fresh free-text email.",
    "coherence": "tight"
  },
